Both are green (exit 0), all 625 cases pass.

**The bug:** in `src/pricing.js`, `orderTotal` applied the tax rate to the *original* price instead of the *discounted* price — even though its own comment said tax should be charged on the discounted amount. Fixed by taxing `discounted` instead of `cents`:

```js
function orderTotal(cents, discountPct, taxRate) {
  const discounted = applyDiscount(cents, discountPct);
  return roundCents(discounted * (1 + taxRate));
}
```

Only 3 of the 625 cases (the "order totals" rows with both a non-zero discount and non-zero tax) exposed this, which is why it was buried. `run-tests.js` and `verify.js` both now exit 0.
